The `public` directory is intended for static assets such as images, fonts, and other files that can be served directly. You can create a subdirectory within `public` to store photos used in the project. Here’s how the contents of the `public` directory can be structured:

- Create a subdirectory named `images` within the `public` directory to store the project images.

The contents of the `public` directory will be as follows:

public/
└── images/
    ├── about-thyme.jpg
    ├── mom3ntum.jpg
    └── boutique.jpg

You can place the respective images in the `images` folder as per your project requirements.